# RC000 Governance Layers

**Authority:** [`docs/rc/RC000-clearstrata-constitution.md`](docs/rc/RC000-clearstrata-constitution.md)

## Supremacy

**RC000 has higher priority than all later RC specifications** (RC009, RC010, RC011, …).

Never modify RC000 unless the user explicitly instructs a constitutional amendment.

## Layer boundaries

| Layer | Owns | Must not |
|---|---|---|
| **Governance** | Issues and **Matters** — facts, evidence, discussion, AI analysis, council responses | Author formal resolutions |
| **Meeting** | Formal **Resolutions** — add, edit, delete, reorder **only before Snapshot Freeze** | Replace voting or skip to execution |
| **Voting** | Democratic approval of frozen motions | Edit resolution text or threshold |
| **Execution** | Tasks, owners, timeline, budget, procurement after approval | Bypass Meeting + Voting |
| **Accountability** | Review, archive, or spawn new Matters | Weaken transparency or audit trail |

## RC010 (official)

- **Name:** RC010 — Meeting Resolution Authoring Before Snapshot
- **Canonical motions:** `meeting_agenda_items` (new flows)
- **Legacy:** `community_resolutions` — read-only / historical; not an authoring source for new governance flows
- **Retired:** Governance 「决议 / Resolution」 authoring tab — do not implement

## Conflict protocol

If a requested implementation conflicts with these boundaries:

1. **Stop before coding**
2. **Explain the conflict** with reference to RC000
3. **Propose a compliant design** (usually: move authoring to MeetingDetail, keep Governance read-only)

Works with [`rc000-implementation-gate.mdc`](rc000-implementation-gate.mdc) and [`clearstrata-constitution.mdc`](clearstrata-constitution.mdc).
